    "turn_text": "Yeah, it's that's some tricky number crunching there. Lawmakers that I've talked to on both sides of the aisle don't think that that's exactly how that's going to work out. And also when you look at the bigger picture, the White House is saying they can either try and pull funding right from this new renegotiated NAFTA, which by the way isn't necessarily a done deal either. Or the other option that the White House is floating is to try and reallocate funds, right, to pull money from other agencies and redirect it so that the president can use that to build his wall. Well, that's not really how it works either. That's money that is allocated by Congress. They take pretty seriously up here that Congress has the power of the purse. When the White House first floated that idea earlier this week, I had one top Republican leader tell me, hey, we may have to get the lawyers. to take a look at that one, because that's just simply not how this is supposed to work, even though the White House thinks that they may be able to pull some money from here, gather up some dollars over there, and somehow collect this pot that the president can use to build a wall when the reality is their justice, not the political will or capital to do that.",
