    "turn_text": "the drips take you very much into a flood and it's all there at once. I do want to make note of an unlikely legislative triumph this week. Criminal justice reform, Mary. This is something President Obama really wanted to do. The Koch brothers were working with the elements in the Obama administration to get this done. It's got a whole set of bipartisan and unlikely allies that were behind it, including Jared Kushner, who deserves a whole lot of credit for elevating this as an issue, bringing the coalitions together, and the fact that we're talking about major sentencing reform, major reform around federal federal guidelines around criminal justice. This is a big deal. It had a lot of powerful enemies, including at one point Mitch McConnell, but the fact that Congress is going to get this done, you know, won't get as many headlines, but it is an intriguing twist on the storylines of paralysis in Congress that there was an attempt and apparently a successful attempt to get this done.",
