    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/7/77296.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 74,
    "turn_text": "senator i want to ask about health care that the texas judge um... over the weekend through uh... bit of a potential legal monkey wrench in in all the plans we know that republicans have been trying to got obama care as they can as you look toward the next congress do you feel like the time is is what what's the best use of democratic strategic energies right now. Is it to work with Republicans on fixes or on making sure that pre-existing conditions, for instance, are covered? Or is it time to just pursue Medicare for all and say, look, the Democrats, as Democrats, we've got a different idea that you would argue is a better idea?",
