  {
    "episode_id": 77296,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/7/77296.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 75,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think we should do both. There is embedded in Obamacare a patient bill of rights. It isn't referred to as that much, but although I think that's the way we should call it. It's the right for your child up to age 26 to be on your policy. It's the right to get the same price for your policy whether you have a preexisting condition. It's the ability to get preventive treatments for free because an ounce of prevention is worth a pound of cure. It's the right to be able to use tax credits to be able to purchase policies if you're a low-income American. I think we need to re-accentuate that bill of rights, lay it out and perhaps even re-pass it into law in that nature or force a vote on it. because i can tell you virtually no republican wants to vote against those things because they are popular throughout the entire spectrum and many of the uh... uh... red or republican regions of the country have benefited more from those rights than anywhere else in america at the same time uh... we have a vision for a much more cost-effective and stress-free system in which you have health care in a seamless simple fashion just by virtue of living in america uh... medicare for all And I talked about this in all my town halls in both my red counties and my blue counties, and people nod their heads. Our healthcare system is massively stressful. We still have bankruptcy for it. We still have confusion over it. People know in their gut we can do this in a much better way.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_04",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Obamacare contains a patient bill of rights.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "The patient bill of rights includes coverage for children up to age 26 on a parent's insurance policy.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Individuals with preexisting conditions have the right to receive the same price for health insurance policies.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Preventive medical treatments should be provided free of charge.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Low-income Americans have the right to use tax credits to purchase health insurance.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "These rights should be re-emphasized and potentially re-enacted into law.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "A universal healthcare system like Medicare for All could provide seamless and stress-free access to healthcare.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "Most Republicans would support these specific provisions due to their popularity.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "Republican-leaning regions have disproportionately benefited from these rights.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "People in both Republican and Democratic communities agree with the need for reform based on personal experience and feedback during town halls.",
